Q: Ionic Angular ion-input doesn&#39;t reset visually when using reactive forms programmatically A: <p>The recommended approach is to keep your business data/state in a service, but create the FormGroup inside the component.</p>
<pre><code>export class SignUpComponent {
  signUpForm = this.fb.group({
    userName: [''],
    email: [''],
    password: ['']
  });

  ionViewWillEnter() {
    this.signUpForm.reset();
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>A FormGroup is a UI-related object whose lifecycle should match the component that owns the view. Storing it in a singleton (providedIn: 'root') means the same form instance is shared across cached Ionic pages, which can lead to synchronization issues with ion-input.</p>
<p>By creating a new FormGroup in each component instance, Angular and Ionic remain in sync, and the inputs are properly cleared when the page is entered.</p>

Q: Can I use C++20 concepts properly in a using declaration? A: <p>Your concept:</p>

<pre><code>template &lt;typename T&gt;
concept i_am_integral = requires { std::is_integral_v&lt;T&gt; == true; };
</code></pre>

<p>does not check if the type is integral. Instead, it checks if comparing <code>std::is_integral_v&lt;T&gt;</code> with <code>true</code> is possible (which is always possible). To fix your code you should just do:</p>

<pre><code>template &lt;typename T&gt;
concept i_am_integral = std::is_integral_v&lt;T&gt;;
</code></pre>
